 by God, regarding this: to send me as soon as possible to the Indies, or another place of infidels, this September. Or if Your Paternity should send me as a slave with the iron at my neck, or grant me this blessed lot of being sold for Christ, though my life is worth little or nothing.",
     "I know that I speak to a Father, and a Father who tenderly loves all his children, though unworthy; for this I add nothing more. I speak more with the heart, and I shall always speak, though with the pen, lest I weary you so. Pardon the excessive boldness of having been so long. The Father covers the defects of children, and of needy children, such as I am. May our Lord give to Your Paternity the completion and the crown of your holy labors, and of the vigilance you have for the good of your subjects."
    ]
   },
   {
    "n": 52,
    "year": 1619,
    "date": "August 3, 1619",
    "place": "Naples",
    "archival": "ARSI, FG 736, 53",
    "excerpt": "I wrote to Your Paternity in months past that I wished to go to Our Lady of Loreto, and I ask whether Your Paternity would grant me this grace: to come barefoot and on foot, and to come by way of Rome to see Your Paternity; but if I come, there shall happen what happened to Jacob, who wrestled a whole night with an Angel — so shall I do with Your Paternity, except that, prostrate upon the ground, I shall never leave Your Paternity until you grant me what I crave and have craved, as Your Paternity knows, though I know myself unworthy of such a grace.",
    "kind": "abridged",
    "full_paras": [
     "I wrote to Your Paternity in months past that I wished to go to Our Lady of Loreto, and I ask whether Your Paternity would grant me this grace: to come barefoot and on foot, and to come by way of Rome to see Your Paternity; but if I come, there shall happen what happened to Jacob, who wrestled a whole night with an Angel — so shall I do with Your Paternity, except that, prostrate upon the ground, I shall never leave Your Paternity until you grant me what I crave and have craved, as Your Paternity knows, though I know myself unworthy of such a grace. Yet I ask this by the merits of our Blessed Father Ignatius and of Blessed Xavier — apropos of those parts whither I wish to go — and, so as to trouble Your Paternity no more, I promise to give you no more trouble, for I hope that with this letter Your Paternity will console me, if you are willing; but in this let not my will be done, but God's, through Your Paternity; and so as to weary Your Paternity no more I make an end, commending myself to your Holy Sacrifices."
    ]
   },
   {
    "n": 53,
    "year": 1620,
    "date": "May 16, 1620",
    "place": "Barletta",
    "archival": "ARSI, FG 736, 153",
    "excerpt": "It is proper to the son to ask of his father, as I have done many times with Your Paternity, my most dear Father — that is, asking many times to be sent to those parts of the Indies for the greater service of God. Though I know myself most unworthy of such a grace on account of my faults and defects, I hope nevertheless in the goodness and mercy of my Lord, who will inspire you in these days of the coming of the Holy Father, that you may fulfill my desire. I find myself in Barletta to this end: to detach myself from my mother, that I may be more ready, as Your Paternity wrote me to do; do with me as you please.",
    "kind": "abridged",
    "full_paras": [
     "It is proper to the son to ask of his father, as I have done many times with Your Paternity, my most dear Father — that is, asking many times to be sent to those parts of the Indies for the greater service of God. Though I know myself most unworthy of such a grace on account of my faults and defects, I hope nevertheless in the goodness and mercy of my Lord, who will inspire you in these days of the coming of the Holy Father, that you may fulfill my desire. I find myself in Barletta to this end: to detach myself from my mother, that I may be more ready, as Your Paternity wrote me to do; do with me as you please. Nothing more; I commend myself most to your holy sacrifices."
    ]
   }
  ]
