  "letters": [
   {
    "n": 40,
    "year": 1618,
    "date": "January 2, 1618",
    "place": "Genoa",
    "archival": "ARSI, FG 735, 1",
    "excerpt": "So ardent is the desire which almighty God gives me to suffer something for His love, that I would greatly fear not to correspond to His loving invitation if I did not make it known to Your Reverence, as to the one who is to accept the invitation — just as some great personage would do, to whom some great King asked for his youngest child, to clothe him in the same livery and garments with which his own son was clothed while he lived in this life, and to treat him in the same manner of life in which he was treated.",
    "kind": "abridged",
    "full_paras": [
     "So ardent is the desire which almighty God gives me to suffer something for His love, that I would greatly fear not to correspond to His loving invitation if I did not make it known to Your Reverence, as to the one who is to accept the invitation — just as some great personage would do, to whom some great King asked for his youngest child, to clothe him in the same livery and garments with which his own son was clothed while he lived in this life, and to treat him in the same manner of life in which he was treated. I say, then, to Your Reverence that I am invited by that supreme King to the same table and to the same manner of life at which His blessed Son fed and in which He lived — that is, to be called to go to the Indies or to some other place where there is hope of suffering great things for His love, even to the shedding of my very blood. Ah, accept, I pray you, accept, Your Reverence, so loving an invitation; and do not refuse, seeing above all how majestic and loving is the Inviter, who is the omnipotent and benign God, and how vile and discourteous is the invited, who is the abominable and ungrateful sinner, Hermete Abellone — with which, in holy indifference, I give myself wholly to Your Reverence, and pray you to deign to commend me to the Lord in your holy sacrifices."
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
