  "dossier": "Wrote 1 letter from Massa (1630) petitioning the General for the foreign missions; requested destination: East Indies (1).",
  "letters": [
   {
    "n": 72,
    "year": 1630,
    "date": "March 2, 1630",
    "place": "Massa",
    "archival": "ARSI, FG 742, 27",
    "excerpt": "His Divine Majesty having, from the very beginning of my entrance, enkindled in my heart a lively and ardent desire to shed my blood in the Indies for His love, and having preserved it in me throughout all the time of my Novitiate; now that I have been destined by holy Obedience to the study of Rhetoric, and with the occasion of the Father Procurator of Ethiopia who was here, and with the fervor of these brothers, I have judged (lest I seem ungrateful to His Divine Majesty for so great a benefit) to make Your Paternity, as my true Father, aware of it, praying you with the greatest affection I can, and for the love of the Most Holy Virgin, that you will number me among the others destined for that mission, although I am most unworthy of it, so that, should the occasion offer itself, you will not fail to console me.",
    "kind": "abridged",
    "full_paras": [
     "His Divine Majesty having, from the very beginning of my entrance, enkindled in my heart a lively and ardent desire to shed my blood in the Indies for His love, and having preserved it in me throughout all the time of my Novitiate; now that I have been destined by holy Obedience to the study of Rhetoric, and with the occasion of the Father Procurator of Ethiopia who was here, and with the fervor of these brothers, I have judged (lest I seem ungrateful to His Divine Majesty for so great a benefit) to make Your Paternity, as my true Father, aware of it, praying you with the greatest affection I can, and for the love of the Most Holy Virgin, that you will number me among the others destined for that mission, although I am most unworthy of it, so that, should the occasion offer itself, you will not fail to console me. With this I close, commending myself to the holy sacrifices of Your Paternity and seeking your blessing."
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
